    - [38;5;153mcheck[39m confirms the account and container are still private.
    - [38;5;153msas r|cw[39m issues a token of at most 60 minutes. It refuses to write to a
      terminal and refuses to sign at all if [38;5;153mcheck[39m fails.
    - [38;5;153mreadback[39m compares the uploaded blobs against the manifest.
    - [38;5;153mpin[39m records the manifest's sha256 in git.
  - [1m[38;5;153mgpu/image-t1-vm.sh[0m runs on the GPU VM: [38;5;153mscan[39m, [38;5;153mpack[39m and [38;5;153mupload[39m (manifest
    uploaded last), plus [38;5;153mfetch[39m.
    - [38;5;153mfetch[39m implements the five checks in §9.3.
    - On any failure it deletes the half-unpacked tree and prints [38;5;153m@@stage [39m
      [38;5;153mprep tarball=fallback reason=…[39m.
    - Notes can call it directly from prep, or treat it as the reference
      implementation of the format.
  - [1mTests:[0m 51 pass against a fake [38;5;153maz[39m and a fake [38;5;153mcurl[39m. They cover:
    - every fallback reason;
    - the SAS never appearing in any command's arguments;
    - a read-only SAS failing to upload.
  - [1mAgainst real Azure:[0m [38;5;153mcheck[39m passes (anonymous gets 409). A real 5-minute
    read SAS was issued and sent straight to [38;5;153m/dev/null[39m, which confirms the
    R4/R5 role assignments work.
  - [1mBug caught before commit:[0m while writing [38;5;153mscan[39m I hit the [38;5;153mgrep | head[39m +
    [38;5;153mpipefail[39m trap again, which would have read a hit as clean. It's fixed,
    and a 50-hit test covers it.

  [1mDecision for you:[0m can I push [38;5;153mgpu/image-t1[39m? It also needs to go to Notes
  with two notes:
